{
  "version": 1,
  "$comment": [
    "T-E2E-ACCOUNT-PREF step 2 (vc69) - the phone downgrade latch (Security B1) and per-account keying (M1). RULE 30.",
    "LANGUAGE-NEUTRAL. Consumer: dnkdialer-android/app/src/test/java/com/dnkdialer/companion/E2eAccountPrefLatchVectorsTest.kt (drives the pure reducer E2eAccountPref over a simulated per-userId store).",
    "users: persisted record per userId at the start ({raw} = a literal unreadable record). userId: the id TokenStore holds (null = not learned). legacy: the vc<=68 local switch (userSetOn = ON and user_set_v2) and the device-level seed-consumed flag.",
    "steps: push (an E2E_PREF body) | pushRaw (a body string, parsed strictly) | userSet on|off (Settings switch after confirm) | keepOff | keepCodeCheck | turnBackOn | refused {op,reason,retryAfterMs?} | signIn <id> | signOut (wipes the current id) | restart (every record re-read from its encoded form) | assert {...}. at = ms clock.",
    "expect/assert: advertised = value used at Accept; prompt = null|PREF_OFF|PAUSED; sent = every frame sent so far as TYPE:value; lastRev (-1 = none, null = no account); pendingOwnWrite on|off|null; notice on|null (one-time raise notice); toasts KIND[:retryAfterMs]; legacyConsumed; users.<id>.exists/advertised/lastRev; peerOffAtAccept = E2eSettings.effectiveMode(advertised, peer OFF).",
    "updatedBy is NEVER an input to the latch: L02 and L16 carry updatedBy=phone with no own write and must latch.",
    "Rows L01-L14 are Ken brief rows 1-14 in order; L15 = the E2E_PREF_REFUSED row; L16 = the hostile-server row; the rest complete the grid.",
    "L27-L31 = the equal-rev rule (Ken ruling 2026-09-25; web twin lib/e2eAccountPref-core.ts applyIncoming). The admin master switch changes effective/pausedByServer WITHOUT bumping rev. rev < lastRev -> dropped. rev == lastRev -> ONLY effective/pausedByServer may move, and only when preference/updatedBy/neverChosen equal the mirror (else dropped); a repeat with nothing moved is dropped. B1 unchanged: a lowered effective still latches and needs the tap; a raise applies at once with no notice (not a preference write). mirror = {preference,effective,pausedByServer} of the stored mirror after the steps."
  ],
